<title>THAILAND: Thai oil firm PTT sees limited baht float impact.</title>
<headline>Thai oil firm PTT sees limited baht float impact.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's state-run Petroleum Authority of Thailand (PTT) said the firm's foreign debt would be hit by the baht's flotation but the overall impact on the company would be limited.</p>
<p>Pichai Chunhavajira, PTT deputy governor for corporate finance and accounting, told reporters that if the baht eased by 10 percent after the de facto devaluation, the company's foreign debt would rise by 1.9 billion baht ($67 million).</p>
</text>
